  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The de-facto standard EEG benchmark for clinical neurological AI — 60,000+ recordings, 7 annotated sub-corpora covering seizure detection, epilepsy classification, artifact typing, and event classification. Explicitly permissive for research and commercial use (no royalties, no field-of-use restrictions). Registration and SSH key required but approved within 24–48 hours. Widely used in deep learning seizure detection literature as the primary evaluation dataset. TUSZ (seizure) and TUEP (epilepsy) sub-corpora are particularly clinically significant. Essential for any team building EEG-based clinical AI.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-05-18",
